, "y0": 0.08236208236208237, "x1": 0.20659340659340658, "y1": 0.09401709401709402}, {"text": "15 marks", "x0": 0.11978021978021978, "y0": 0.11732711732711733, "x1": 0.1989010989010989, "y1": 0.12742812742812742}, {"text": "Attempt Question 1", "x0": 0.11868131868131868, "y0": 0.13364413364413363, "x1": 0.2868131868131868, "y1": 0.14685314685314685}, {"text": "Allow about 40 minutes for this section", "x0": 0.11868131868131868, "y0": 0.15073815073815075, "x1": 0.45604395604395603, "y1": 0.16083916083916083}, {"text": "Answer the question on pages 2~7 of the Paper | Writing Booklet. Extra writing booklets are", "x0": 0.11978021978021978, "y0": 0.18337218337218336, "x1": 0.8791208791208791, "y1": 0.19658119658119658}, {"text": "available.", "x0": 0.11978021978021978, "y0": 0.20124320124320125, "x1": 0.1956043956043956, "y1": 0.21056721056721056}, {"text": "Your answers will be assessed on how well you:", "x0": 0.14395604395604394, "y0": 0.23154623154623155, "x1": 0.5351648351648352, "y1": 0.24397824397824397}, {"text": "* demonstrate understanding of the way perceptions of discovery are shaped in and", "x0": 0.14285714285714285, "y0": 0.2501942501942502, "x1": 0.856043956043956, "y1": 0.2634032634032634}, {"text": "through texts", "x0": 0.16703296703296702, "y0": 0.2680652680652681, "x1": 0.2714285714285714, "y1": 0.2804972804972805}, {"text": "\u00a9 describe, explain and analyse the relationship between language, text and context", "x0": 0.14285714285714285, "y0": 0.2874902874902875, "x1": 0.8252747252747252, "y1": 0.3006993006993007}, {"text": "Question 1 (15 marks)", "x0": 0.11978021978021978, "y0": 0.33255633255633255, "x1": 0.30439560439560437, "y1": 0.34498834498834496}, {"text": "Examine Texts 1, 2 and 3 on pages 2-6 of the Stimulus Booklet carefully and then answer the", "x0": 0.11978021978021978, "y0": 0.36596736596736595, "x1": 0.8791208791208791, "y1": 0.3791763791763792}, {"text": "questions below.", "x0": 0.11868131868131868, "y0": 0.38306138306138304, "x1": 0.25384615384615383, "y1": 0.3954933954933955}, {"text": "Text 1 \u2014 Website interview", "x0": 0.11868131868131868, "y0": 0.43278943278943277, "x1": 0.35934065934065934, "y1": 0.4428904428904429}, {"text": "(a) How does Text | explore the relationship between photography and discovery?", "x0": 0.11978021978021978, "y0": 0.466977466977467, "x1": 0.8087912087912088, "y1": 0.4794094794094794}, {"text": "Text 2\u2014 Poem", "x0": 0.11868131868131868, "y0": 0.515928515928516, "x1": 0.25164835164835164, "y1": 0.526029526029526}, {"text": "(b) How does the poet use imagery to invite the reader to imagine the experience of", "x0": 0.11978021978021978, "y0": 0.5493395493395493, "x1": 0.8098901098901099, "y1": 0.5625485625485626}, {"text": "discovery?", "x0": 0.16703296703296702, "y0": 0.5664335664335665, "x1": 0.25274725274725274, "y1": 0.5788655788655789}, {"text": "Text 1 and Text 2 \u2014 Website interview and Poem", "x0": 0.11868131868131868, "y0": 0.6161616161616161, "x1": 0.5428571428571428, "y1": 0.6262626262626263}, {"text": "(c) Compare the ways in which Text | and Text 2 portray the feelings associated", "x0": 0.11978021978021978, "y0": 0.6495726495726496, "x1": 0.8076923076923077, "y1": 0.6627816627816627}, {"text": "with discovery.", "x0": 0.16703296703296702, "y0": 0.6658896658896659, "x1": 0.29010989010989013, "y1": 0.679098679098679}, {"text": "Text 3 \u2014 Nonfiction extract", "x0": 0.11868131868131868, "y0": 0.7156177156177156, "x1": 0.36153846153846153, "y1": 0.7257187257187258}, {"text": "(d) Analyse how Text 3 develops the idea that altered perspectives lead to discovery.", "x0": 0.11978021978021978, "y0": 0.749028749028749, "x1": 0.8076923076923077, "y1": 0.7622377622377622}], [{"text": "Section II", "x0": 0.11978021978021978, "y0": 0.08236208236208237, "x1": 0.2164835164835165, "y1": 0.09401709401709402}, {"text": "15 marks", "x0": 0.11978021978021978, "y0": 0.11732711732711733, "x1": 0.1989010989010989, "y1": 0.12742812742812742}, {"text": "Attempt Question 2", "x0": 0.11868131868131868, "y0": 0.13364413364413363, "x1": 0.2879120879120879, "y1": 0.14685314685314685}, {"text": "Allow about 40 minutes for this section", "x0": 0.11868131868131868, "y0": 0.15073815073815075, "x1": 0.45604395604395603, "y1": 0.16083916083916083}, {"text": "Answer the question on pages 8-15 of the Paper | Writing Booklet. Extra writing booklets are", "x0": 0.11978021978021978, "y0": 0.18337218337218336, "x1": 0.8791208791208791, "y1": 0.19658119658119658}, {"text": "available.", "x0": 0.11978021978021978, "y0": 0.20124320124320125, "x1": 0.1956043956043956, "y1": 0.21056721056721056}, {"text": "Your answer will be assessed on how well you:", "x0": 0.14395604395604394, "y0": 0.23076923076923078, "x1": 0.5274725274725275, "y1": 0.24397824397824397}, {"text": "express understanding of discovery in the context of your studies", "x0": 0.16703296703296702, "y0": 0.2501942501942502, "x1": 0.6945054945054945, "y1": 0.2634032634032634}, {"text": "organise, develop and express ideas using language appropriate to audience, purpose", "x0": 0.16703296703296702, "y0": 0.2703962703962704, "x1": 0.856043956043956, "y1": 0.2836052836052836}, {"text": "and context", "x0": 0.16703296703296702, "y0": 0.28826728826728826, "x1": 0.25934065934065936, "y1": 0.2975912975912976}, {"text": "Question 2 (15 marks)", "x0": 0.11978021978021978, "y0": 0.33255633255633255, "x1": 0.30439560439560437, "y1": 0.34498834498834496}, {"text": "Compose an imaginative text that explores two different perspectives on discovery.", "x0": 0.11868131868131868, "y0": 0.36596736596736595, "x1": 0.7945054945054945, "y1": 0.3791763791763792}, {"text": "Use the following quotation within your response.", "x0": 0.11978021978021978, "y0": 0.39937839937839936, "x1": 0.5252747252747253, "y1": 0.4125874125874126}, {"text": "\u2018it is terrifying and magnificent, familiar and utterly alien\u2019", "x0": 0.24175824175824176, "y0": 0.4491064491064491, "x1": 0.7098901098901099, "y1": 0.46231546231546233}, {"text": "Please turn over", "x0": 0.42967032967032964, "y0": 0.5167055167055167, "x1": 0.5692307692307692, "y1": 0.5268065268065268}], [{"text": "Section IT", "x0": 0.11978021978021978, "y0": 0.08236208236208237, "x1": 0.22527472527472528, "y1": 0.09401709401709402}, {"text": "15 marks", "x0": 0.11978021978021978, "y0": 0.11732711732711733, "x1": 0.1989010989010989, "y1": 0.12742812742812742}, {"text": "Attempt Question 3", "x0": 0.11868131868131868, "y0": 0.13364413364413363, "x1": 0.2879120879120879, "y1": 0.14685314685314685}, {"text": "Allow about 40 minutes for this section", "x0": 0.11868131868131868, "y0": 0.15073815073815075, "x1": 0.45604395604395603, "y1": 0.16083916083916083}, {"text": "Answer the question on pages 16-24 of the Paper 1 Writing Booklet. Extra writing booklets", "x0": 0.11978021978021978, "y0": 0.18337218337218336, "x1": 0.8791208791208791, "y1": 0.19658119658119658}, {"text": "are available.", "x0": 0.11978021978021978, "y0": 0.20046620046620048, "x1": 0.22527472527472528, "y1": 0.21056721056721056}, {"text": "Your answer will be assessed on how well you:", "x0": 0.14395604395604394, "y0": 0.23154623154623155, "x1": 0.5274725274725275, "y1": 0.24397824397824397}, {"text": "demonstrate understanding of the concept of discovery in the context of your study", "x0": 0.16703296703296702, "y0": 0.2501942501942502, "x1": 0.8406593406593407, "y1": 0.2634032634032634}, {"text": "e analyse, explain and assess the ways discovery is represented in a variety of texts", "x0": 0.14285714285714285, "y0": 0.2703962703962704, "x1": 0.8263736263736263, "y1": 0.2836052836052836}, {"text": "\u00a9 organise, develop and express ideas using language appropriate to audience, purpose", "x0": 0.14285714285714285, "y0": 0.2905982905982906, "x1": 0.856043956043956, "y1": 0.3038073038073038}, {"text": "and context", "x0": 0.16703296703296702, "y0": 0.3076923076923077, "x1": 0.25934065934065936, "y1": 0.317016317016317}, {"text": "Question 3 (15 marks)", "x0": 0.11978021978021978, "y0": 0.35275835275835277, "x1": 0.30439560439560437, "y1": 0.3651903651903652}, {"text": "Discovery is not always finding the new, nor is it always a joy.", "x0": 0.11978021978021978, "y0": 0.3861693861693862, "x1": 0.6307692307692307, "y1": 0.39937839937839936}, {"text": "To what extent do the texts you have studied reflect this view of discovery?", "x0": 0.11868131868131868, "y0": 0.4195804195804196, "x1": 0.734065934065934, "y1": 0.43278943278943277}, {"text": "In your response, refer to your prescribed text and ONE related text of your own choosing.", "x0": 0.11978021978021978, "y0": 0.452991452991453, "x1": 0.856043956043956, "y1": 0.4662004662004662}, {"text": "The prescribed texts are listed on page 7 of the Stimulus Booklet.", "x0": 0.11868131868131868, "y0": 0.48562548562548563, "x1": 0.6505494505494506, "y1": 0.4988344988344988}, {"text": "End of paper", "x0": 0.44285714285714284, "y0": 0.5532245532245532, "x1": 0.5560439560439561, "y1": 0.5664335664335665}, {"text": "(\u00a9 2018 NSW Edueation Standards Authority", "x0": 0.3824175824175824, "y0": 0.9673659673659674, "x1": 0.6164835164835165, "y1": 0.9751359751359752}], [{"text": "NSW Education Standards Authority", "x0": 0.11978021978021978, "y0": 0.19114219114219114, "x1": 0.4725274725274725, "y1": 0.20512820512820512}, {"text": "2018 | HIGHER SCHOOL CERTIFICATE EXAMINATION", "x0": 0.12747252747252746, "y0": 0.31002331002331, "x1": 0.5857142857142857, "y1": 0.32323232323232326}, {"text": "English (Standard)", "x0": 0.12307692307692308, "y0": 0.35120435120435123, "x1": 0.554945054945055, "y1": 0.38694638694638694}, {"text": "and English (Advanced)", "x0": 0.12087912087912088, "y0": 0.3962703962703963, "x1": 0.6835164835164835, "y1": 0.432012432012432}, {"text": "Paper 1 \u2014 Area of Study", "x0": 0.12197802197802197, "y0": 0.4662004662004662, "x1": 0.5417582417582417, "y1": 0.49106449106449107}, {"text": "Stimulus Booklet for Section |", "x0": 0.11978021978021978, "y0": 0.5275835275835276, "x1": 0.5945054945054945, "y1": 0.5477855477855478}, {"text": "and", "x0": 0.11868131868131868, "y0": 0.5594405594405595, "x1": 0.18021978021978022, "y1": 0.5796425796425796}, {"text": "List of prescribed texts for Section Ill", "x0": 0.12087912087912088, "y0": 0.5905205905205905, "x1": 0.7076923076923077, "y1": 0.6153846153846154}, {"text": "Pages", "x0": 0.8252747252747252, "y0": 0.6278166278166278, "x1": 0.8791208791208791, "y1": 0.6410256410256411}, {"text": "Section I + Text 1 \u2014 Website interview 2-3", "x0": 0.11868131868131868, "y0": 0.662004662004662, "x1": 0.8791208791208791, "y1": 0.6721056721056721}, {"text": "Text 2 \u2014 4", "x0": 0.2824175824175824, "y0": 0.696969696969697, "x1": 0.8791208791208791, "y1": 0.7070707070707071}, {"text": "+ Text 3 - Nonfiction extract", "x0": 0.2681318681318681, "y0": 0.7319347319347319, "x1": 0.521978021978022, "y1": 0.7420357420357421}, {"text": "Section Ill + List of prescribed texts ....", "x0": 0.11868131868131868, "y0": 0.7661227661227661, "x1": 0.521978021978022, "y1": 0.7793317793317793}, {"text": "1021", "x0": 0.08241758241758242, "y0": 0.9463869463869464, "x1": 0.11428571428571428, "y1": 0.9549339549339549}], [{"text": "Section I", "x0": 0.11868131868131868, "y0": 0.08236208236208237, "x1": 0.2076923076923077, "y1": 0.0947940947940948}, {"text": "Text 1 \u2014 Website interview", "x0": 0.11868131868131868, "y0": 0.11499611499611499, "x1": 0.36043956043956044, "y1": 0.1258741258741259}, {"text": "Digital magazine Designboom (DB) interviewed American photographer Steve McCurry (SM)", "x0": 0.11868131868131868, "y0": 0.14763014763014762, "x1": 0.8802197802197802, "y1": 0.16083916083916083}, {"text": "at his solo exhibition in Mexico City, 2015.", "x0": 0.11868131868131868, "y0": 0.16472416472416473, "x1": 0.4725274725274725, "y1": 0.17793317793317792}, {"text": "Text 1 continues on page 3", "x0": 0.38461538461538464, "y0": 0.9036519036519036, "x1": 0.6142857142857143, "y1": 0.9168609168609169}], [{"text": "Text | (continued)", "x0": 0.11868131868131868, "y0": 0.08158508158508158, "x1": 0.2692307692307692, "y1": 0.09324009324009325}, {"text": "End of Text 1", "x0": 0.44065934065934065, "y0": 0.8329448329448329, "x1": 0.5582417582417583, "y1": 0.8438228438228438}], [{"text": "Day", "x0": 0.7252747252747253, "y0": 0.8275058275058275, "x1": 0.7604395604395604, "y1": 0.8368298368298368}, {"text": "* tawdry", "x0": 0.2549450549450549, "y0": 0.8609168609168609, "x1": 0.3120879120879121, "y1": 0.8725718725718725}, {"text": "showy but poor quality", "x0": 0.3802197802197802, "y0": 0.8609168609168609, "x1": 0.5362637362637362, "y1": 0.8725718725718725}, {"text": "vermilion", "x0": 0.26703296703296703, "y0": 0.878010878010878, "x1": 0.33076923076923076, "y1": 0.8865578865578866}, {"text": "bright red", "x0": 0.3802197802197802, "y0": 0.878010878010878, "x1": 0.44945054945054946, "y1": 0.8888888888888888}, {"text": "unit of measurement for the depth of water", "x0": 0.3813186813186813, "y0": 0.8873348873348873, "x1": 0.6703296703296703, "y1": 0.9114219114219114}, {"text": "-4-", "x0": 0.47912087912087914, "y0": 0.9432789432789432, "x1": 0.5208791208791209, "y1": 0.9533799533799534}], [{"text": "Text 3 \u2014 Nonfiction extract", "x0": 0.11868131868131868, "y0": 0.08158508158508158, "x1": 0.36153846153846153, "y1": 0.09168609168609168}, {"text": "Points of view", "x0": 0.11978021978021978, "y0": 0.13597513597513597, "x1": 0.23956043956043957, "y1": 0.14607614607614608}, {"text": "Views, it is alleged, came into being on 26 April 1336. Before that date, on which the Italian", "x0": 0.11978021978021978, "y0": 0.16394716394716394, "x1": 0.8791208791208791, "y1": 0.17715617715617715}, {"text": "poet Petrarch climbed Mont Ventoux in Provence simply to look at what could be seen from", "x0": 0.11978021978021978, "y0": 0.18104118104118105, "x1": 0.8791208791208791, "y1": 0.19425019425019424}, {"text": "the top, there\u2019s no evidence that anyone \u2014 any hermit or cowherd, any pilgrim or traveller \u2014 had", "x0": 0.11978021978021978, "y0": 0.19425019425019424, "x1": 0.8791208791208791, "y1": 0.21367521367521367}, {"text": "ever looked out and down on the world just for the poetic feelings that might be aroused in", "x0": 0.11868131868131868, "y0": 0.21445221445221446, "x1": 0.8791208791208791, "y1": 0.22766122766122765}, {"text": "them by what they saw. Or even at a lake or seascape. They must have, on countless occasions,", "x0": 0.11978021978021978, "y0": 0.23154623154623155, "x1": 0.8791208791208791, "y1": 0.24397824397824397}, {"text": "but since there\u2019s no evidence of it, the British art historian Kenneth Clark declared Petrarch", "x0": 0.11868131868131868, "y0": 0.24786324786324787, "x1": 0.8791208791208791, "y1": 0.2595182595182595}, {"text": "to be the first man to climb a mountain for its own sake, and to enjoy the view from the top.", "x0": 0.11978021978021978, "y0": 0.2641802641802642, "x1": 0.8791208791208791, "y1": 0.2773892773892774}, {"text": "Indeed, he declared him to be the first modern man. Nobody has bothered to argue with him.", "x0": 0.11978021978021978, "y0": 0.2804972804972805, "x1": 0.8725274725274725, "y1": 0.2937062937062937}, {"text": "... Petrarch himself claimed that he\u2019d climbed the highest mountain in that part of France for", "x0": 0.11978021978021978, "y0": 0.30924630924630925, "x1": 0.8802197802197802, "y1": 0.32245532245532244}, {"text": "no other reason than to see what so great an elevation had to offer. He was dazed, he wrote,", "x0": 0.11978021978021978, "y0": 0.32556332556332557, "x1": 0.8791208791208791, "y1": 0.33877233877233875}, {"text": "by the vast sweep of the view spread out before him. He claimed, as no mountain climber had", "x0": 0.11868131868131868, "y0": 0.34265734265734266, "x1": 0.8791208791208791, "y1": 0.35586635586635584}, {"text": "ever claimed (in writing) before him, to have been \u2018bent on pleasure\u2019 and anxious that his", "x0": 0.11868131868131868, "y0": 0.358974358974359, "x1": 0.8791208791208791, "y1": 0.37218337218337216}, {"text": "enjoyment should be \u2018unalloyed\u2019*. (Leisure in a nutshell, really.) Before Petrarch, it seems,", "x0": 0.11868131868131868, "y0": 0.37606837606837606, "x1": 0.8791208791208791, "y1": 0.38927738927738925}, {"text": "people surveyed the scene from an elevated position for a purpose: on the watch for enemy", "x0": 0.11978021978021978, "y0": 0.3923853923853924, "x1": 0.8791208791208791, "y1": 0.40559440559440557}, {"text": "troops, to search for lost sheep, to keep an eye on what the neighbours were doing. In many", "x0": 0.11978021978021978, "y0": 0.4094794094794095, "x1": 0.8791208791208791, "y1": 0.4226884226884227}, {"text": "parts of the world, people also climbed mountains to commune with the gods.", "x0": 0.11978021978021978, "y0": 0.4257964257964258, "x1": 0.7505494505494505, "y1": 0.439005439005439}, {"text": "Nowadays, 700 years after Petrarch, looking at a view for its own sake is something we all", "x0": 0.11978021978021978, "y0": 0.45454545454545453, "x1": 0.8791208791208791, "y1": 0.4677544677544678}, {"text": "indulge in whenever we get the chance. Planeloads, indeed trainloads of people arrive in", "x0": 0.11978021978021978, "y0": 0.47086247086247085, "x1": 0.8791208791208791, "y1": 0.4840714840714841}, {"text": "Darjeeling every day to look at the view \u2014 nothing else, just look at it. At home we design and", "x0": 0.11978021978021978, "y0": 0.48795648795648794, "x1": 0.8791208791208791, "y1": 0.5011655011655012}, {"text": "build houses specifically to provide what is termed a \u201cstare view\u2019 from the living room and", "x0": 0.11868131868131868, "y0": 0.4972804972804973, "x1": 0.8791208791208791, "y1": 0.5205905205905206}, {"text": "possibly a bedroom or two, although rarely any other part of the house \u2014 a bathroom with a", "x0": 0.11978021978021978, "y0": 0.5213675213675214, "x1": 0.8802197802197802, "y1": 0.5345765345765345}, {"text": "view, for instance, is still considered an amusing eccentricity. When I\u2019m at the weekender, at", "x0": 0.11978021978021978, "y0": 0.5376845376845377, "x1": 0.8791208791208791, "y1": 0.5508935508935509}, {"text": "the desk in the living room, I often write looking at a nicely framed view of forested hills: it", "x0": 0.11978021978021978, "y0": 0.554001554001554, "x1": 0.8802197802197802, "y1": 0.5672105672105672}, {"text": "provides a sort of counterpoint to the busyness in my head, keeping me on the alert. Despite the", "x0": 0.11978021978021978, "y0": 0.5710955710955711, "x1": 0.8791208791208791, "y1": 0.5843045843045843}, {"text": "fact that, as far as I can see, nothing much ever happens out there \u2014 a pair of black cockatoos", "x0": 0.11978021978021978, "y0": 0.5874125874125874, "x1": 0.8791208791208791, "y1": 0.6006216006216006}, {"text": "might swoop past, screeching amicably, a curtain of rain might drift in from the west, obscuring", "x0": 0.11978021978021978, "y0": 0.6045066045066045, "x1": 0.8791208791208791, "y1": 0.6177156177156177}, {"text": "the valley \u2014 looking at this vista provides me with a kind of second self without my moving", "x0": 0.11978021978021978, "y0": 0.6208236208236209, "x1": 0.8791208791208791, "y1": 0.634032634032634}, {"text": "an inch.", "x0": 0.11978021978021978, "y0": 0.6386946386946387, "x1": 0.1813186813186813, "y1": 0.6480186480186481}, {"text": "In Australia we have lookouts where you not only may but indeed are encouraged to stand and", "x0": 0.11978021978021978, "y0": 0.6658896658896659, "x1": 0.8791208791208791, "y1": 0.679098679098679}, {"text": "stare. Local councils often signpost them so that tourists driving by can stop, point their mobile", "x0": 0.11978021978021978, "y0": 0.682983682983683, "x1": 0.8791208791208791, "y1": 0.6961926961926962}, {"text": "phones at them and drive on inwardly refreshed. What is it, though, that traditionally refreshes", "x0": 0.11978021978021978, "y0": 0.6993006993006993, "x1": 0.8791208791208791, "y1": 0.7125097125097125}, {"text": "us at a lookout?", "x0": 0.11978021978021978, "y0": 0.7171717171717171, "x1": 0.24725274725274726, "y1": 0.7264957264957265}, {"text": "In a sense, every view offers us a hint of the sublime, surely \u2014 a rush of terror while staying", "x0": 0.11978021978021978, "y0": 0.7443667443667443, "x1": 0.8791208791208791, "y1": 0.7575757575757576}, {"text": "safe. Every view contains a dash, however faint, of the epiphanic**. Even an ocean view on", "x0": 0.11978021978021978, "y0": 0.7614607614607615, "x1": 0.8791208791208791, "y1": 0.7746697746697747}, {"text": "a calm, sunny day can provoke thoughts of what lurks beneath the waves: on the one hand,", "x0": 0.11978021978021978, "y0": 0.7777777777777778, "x1": 0.8791208791208791, "y1": 0.790986790986791}, {"text": "nothing at all, unending gloom; on the other, death from drowning, death from a lurking", "x0": 0.11978021978021978, "y0": 0.7948717948717948, "x1": 0.8791208791208791, "y1": 0.8080808080808081}, {"text": "stonefish, death from a shark attack, death from a giant squid. Monsters or nothingness: in", "x0": 0.11978021978021978, "y0": 0.8111888111888111, "x1": 0.8791208791208791, "y1": 0.8243978243978244}, {"text": "either case oblivion. Yet here on the beach or the headland we\u2019re untouchable. On the edge of", "x0": 0.11868131868131868, "y0": 0.8282828282828283, "x1": 0.8813186813186813, "y1": 0.8414918414918415}, {"text": "an escarpment in the Alps it\u2019s much the same thing: staring out into the void we have thoughts", "x0": 0.11978021978021978, "y0": 0.8445998445998446, "x1": 0.8791208791208791, "y1": 0.8578088578088578}, {"text": "Text 3 continues on page 6", "x0": 0.38461538461538464, "y0": 0.8997668997668997, "x1": 0.6142857142857143, "y1": 0.912975912975913}], [{"text": "Text 3 (continued)", "x0": 0.11868131868131868, "y0": 0.08158508158508158, "x1": 0.2692307692307692, "y1": 0.09401709401709402}, {"text": "of death from cold, or death from a fall, or death from an avalanche, or death from a suicidal", "x0": 0.11868131868131868, "y0": 0.13597513597513597, "x1": 0.8791208791208791, "y1": 0.14763014763014762}, {"text": "leap, or, in the Himalayas, death from a sudden landslide or a pouncing snow leopard (rare but", "x0": 0.11978021978021978, "y0": 0.1522921522921523, "x1": 0.8802197802197802, "y1": 0.1655011655011655}, {"text": "imaginable). Looking, we are two people. This is literally ecstasy: standing outside yourself in", "x0": 0.11978021978021978, "y0": 0.16394716394716394, "x1": 0.8824175824175824, "y1": 0.18803418803418803}, {"text": "a direct sense.", "x0": 0.11978021978021978, "y0": 0.1857031857031857, "x1": 0.23186813186813188, "y1": 0.1958041958041958}, {"text": "\u2018A view can also provide a narrative, which looking across a plain cannot, especially if it\u2019s", "x0": 0.11978021978021978, "y0": 0.21445221445221446, "x1": 0.8791208791208791, "y1": 0.22766122766122765}, {"text": "carefully framed, as many of the panoramas offered by our lookouts are. Some even have a", "x0": 0.11868131868131868, "y0": 0.23076923076923078, "x1": 0.8791208791208791, "y1": 0.24397824397824397}, {"text": "touch of theatre in the broadest sense of the word. The first view I can remember ever seeing", "x0": 0.11978021978021978, "y0": 0.24786324786324787, "x1": 0.8791208791208791, "y1": 0.26107226107226106}, {"text": "as a child was at Echo Point in the Blue Mountains west of Sydney: hardly a drop at all by", "x0": 0.11978021978021978, "y0": 0.2641802641802642, "x1": 0.8791208791208791, "y1": 0.2773892773892774}, {"text": "Nepalese or Swiss standards, but by my standards, as a six-year-old local, spine-tingling. It", "x0": 0.11978021978021978, "y0": 0.2804972804972805, "x1": 0.8791208791208791, "y1": 0.2937062937062937}, {"text": "wasn\u2019t just a matter of the sheer cliffs, the certainty of death if you slipped, the hostile bush-", "x0": 0.11978021978021978, "y0": 0.2975912975912976, "x1": 0.8791208791208791, "y1": 0.3108003108003108}, {"text": "covered landscapes empty of life yet at the same time seething with death-dealing animals", "x0": 0.11868131868131868, "y0": 0.3139083139083139, "x1": 0.8593406593406593, "y1": 0.3271173271173271}, {"text": "well, snakes and spiders, anyway. It was the stories of the first explorers from a century and", "x0": 0.11978021978021978, "y0": 0.331002331002331, "x1": 0.8791208791208791, "y1": 0.3442113442113442}, {"text": "a half before, the thoughts of convict chain gangs, the questions about how the people on the", "x0": 0.11978021978021978, "y0": 0.3473193473193473, "x1": 0.8791208791208791, "y1": 0.3605283605283605}, {"text": "farms we could make out far below us first settled there, how they got there, where the road", "x0": 0.11978021978021978, "y0": 0.3644133644133644, "x1": 0.8791208791208791, "y1": 0.3776223776223776}, {"text": "was and who had built it.", "x0": 0.11978021978021978, "y0": 0.3815073815073815, "x1": 0.321978021978022, "y1": 0.39083139083139085}, {"text": "There was a narrative, in other words, to dwell on, as there inevitably is along any coastline", "x0": 0.11868131868131868, "y0": 0.4094794094794095, "x1": 0.8791208791208791, "y1": 0.4226884226884227}, {"text": "as well: of smugglers and shipwrecks, adventure, invasions, arrivals and departures.", "x0": 0.11978021978021978, "y0": 0.4257964257964258, "x1": 0.8791208791208791, "y1": 0.439005439005439}, {"text": "Again, you don\u2019t get that \u2014 not really, not quite so dramatically \u2014 on the flat. On the flat \u2014 out", "x0": 0.11978021978021978, "y0": 0.4428904428904429, "x1": 0.8791208791208791, "y1": 0.4560994560994561}, {"text": "walking in the country, for instance, looking at green folds in the landscape, perhaps at a river", "x0": 0.11978021978021978, "y0": 0.4592074592074592, "x1": 0.8802197802197802, "y1": 0.47241647241647244}, {"text": "\u2014 you might get a pleasing prospect or two, but that\u2019s not a view", "x0": 0.11868131868131868, "y0": 0.4763014763014763, "x1": 0.6406593406593407, "y1": 0.48951048951048953}, {"text": "I don\u2019t believe that we enjoy views, even commanding views (as they are revealingly called),", "x0": 0.11978021978021978, "y0": 0.5042735042735043, "x1": 0.8791208791208791, "y1": 0.5174825174825175}, {"text": "principally because of the power they endow us with ... Yes, in some cases we might have the", "x0": 0.11978021978021978, "y0": 0.5213675213675214, "x1": 0.8791208791208791, "y1": 0.5345765345765345}, {"text": "illusion of omnipotence***: looking out and down (as we do as a rule \u2014 rarely up) we see the", "x0": 0.11978021978021978, "y0": 0.5376845376845377, "x1": 0.8791208791208791, "y1": 0.5508935508935509}, {"text": "world in miniature, like a model landscape we can refashion as we wish. In general, though, I", "x0": 0.11978021978021978, "y0": 0.554001554001554, "x1": 0.8791208791208791, "y1": 0.5672105672105672}, {"text": "think it\u2019s subtler than that. I think views are a permitted way of looking because of the added", "x0": 0.11978021978021978, "y0": 0.5710955710955711, "x1": 0.8791208791208791, "y1": 0.5843045843045843}, {"text": "pleasures they afford without inciting us to break rules or behave badly. Staring at the night", "x0": 0.11978021978021978, "y0": 0.5874125874125874, "x1": 0.8791208791208791, "y1": 0.6006216006216006}, {"text": "sky is similar: it both amplifies your sense of who you are and annihilates you in the same", "x0": 0.11978021978021978, "y0": 0.6045066045066045, "x1": 0.8791208791208791, "y1": 0.6177156177156177}, {"text": "instant \u2014 it is terrifying and magnificent, familiar and utterly alien. It is perfectly acceptable", "x0": 0.11978021978021978, "y0": 0.6208236208236209, "x1": 0.8791208791208791, "y1": 0.634032634032634}, {"text": "to stare at it in wonder. Not for long, of course, any more than you can stare at the sea or the", "x0": 0.11978021978021978, "y0": 0.6379176379176379, "x1": 0.8791208791208791, "y1": 0.6511266511266511}, {"text": "view from Mont Ventoux for long before you start to feel empty and want to go home.", "x0": 0.11978021978021978, "y0": 0.6542346542346542, "x1": 0.8131868131868132, "y1": 0.6674436674436675}, {"text": "nothing more boring than the infinite. And spelling it with a capital \u2018I\u2019 doesn\u2019t make it any", "x0": 0.11978021978021978, "y0": 0.6713286713286714, "x1": 0.8791208791208791, "y1": 0.6845376845376845}, {"text": "more appealing.", "x0": 0.11978021978021978, "y0": 0.6884226884226884, "x1": 0.24725274725274726, "y1": 0.7008547008547008}, {"text": "RoseErT DEsSAIX", "x0": 0.7450549450549451, "y0": 0.7117327117327117, "x1": 0.8791208791208791, "y1": 0.721056721056721}, {"text": "Edited extract from The Pleasures of Leisure", "x0": 0.5153846153846153, "y0": 0.728049728049728, "x1": 0.8791208791208791, "y1": 0.7412587412587412}, {"text": "* unalloyed pure", "x0": 0.13846153846153847, "y0": 0.7676767676767676, "x1": 0.3153846153846154, "y1": 0.7777777777777778}, {"text": "** epiphanic sudden insight into an essential truth", "x0": 0.12967032967032968, "y0": 0.7847707847707848, "x1": 0.5351648351648352, "y1": 0.7948717948717948}, {"text": "omnipotence all-seeing and all-knowing", "x0": 0.14945054945054945, "y0": 0.8018648018648019, "x1": 0.46483516483516485, "y1": 0.811965811965812}, {"text": "Extract from The Pleasure of Leisure by Robert Dessaix.", "x0": 0.545054945054945, "y0": 0.8337218337218337, "x1": 0.8758241758241758, "y1": 0.8430458430458431}, {"text": "Reproduced with permission from the Transcripter Ply", "x0": 0.5615384615384615, "y0": 0.8453768453768454, "x1": 0.8791208791208791, "y1": 0.8547008547008547}, {"text": "Limited Trading as Australian Literary Management", "x0": 0.5791208791208792, "y0": 0.8562548562548562, "x1": 0.8791208791208791, "y1": 0.8655788655788655}, {"text": "End of Text 3", "x0": 0.44065934065934065, "y0": 0.8997668997668997, "x1": 0.5582417582417583, "y1": 0.9098679098679099}], [{"text": "Section III", 